-- The shapes a command heading can take.


-- Curly arguments, with a `:tail{...}` chain.
[\module:over{R}:with{S}]
Declares: M
when: R, S is \set
Documented:
. called: "module over $R?$ with $S?$"
Id: "c259c92b-6f91-4b41-95d6-ad435836be8c"


-- A `?` marks an optional tail; a definition is registered for each
-- combination, so `\norm`, `\norm:on{V}` and `\norm:on{V}:with{P}` all resolve.
[\norm:?on{V}:?with{P}]
Declares: N
when: V, P is \set
Documented:
. called: "norm"
Id: "fe2341bc-c21b-4a78-8cec-1089da4af4f2"


-- A spec-infix command, `\:name:/`, is sugar for a command whose left operand
-- is the symbol being defined. That symbol is stated on the `Declares:` target,
-- and so may not appear in `when:`.
[A \:subset:/ B]
Declares: A is \set
when: B is \set
Requires:
. capability: x_ "in" A :-> x_ "in" B
Documented:
. written: "A? \subseteq B?"
Id: "2acb059b-46d8-4cca-a4fc-aaae4bf9b135"


-- An optional tail on a spec-infix heading.
[A \:contained:?within{U}:/ B]
Declares: A is \set
when:
. U is \set
. B \:subset:/ U
Documented:
. written: "A? \subseteq_{U?} B?"
Id: "07e8e611-08e0-490d-8f62-030af8f9e7e8"


[\reals.set]
Defines: R := \set@{r : ...}
Documented:
. called: "the set of reals"
Id: "8ec56012-f504-44d1-a1eb-04301de15075"


-- A mapping parameter picks one input of a mapping declared in another curly
-- group, so `\partial:of{f(x_)}:in{f.x_}` names a partial derivative.
[\partial:of{f(x_)}:in{f.x_}]
Defines: v is \real
when: f is \function:on{\reals.set}:to{\reals.set}
Documented:
. called: "partial derivative"
Id: "086ac065-d2bf-41a9-a291-34a747dc2e6d"


-- A subset relation is a spec fact, and the `Requires:` capability above lets
-- membership in the smaller set reduce to membership in the larger one.
Theorem:
given:
. A is \set
. B is \set
. x is \element:of{A}
where: A \:subset:/ B
then: x "in"? B
Documented:
. called: "a subset passes membership along"
Id: "b13ec219-c558-42b6-8d28-57d8ea23126e"
